-- title:
--   Places over a node separated by node-ring values
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a nonzero level $N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$; fix modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr` (the bivariate reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ factors as $(C(X)^q - X)(C(X) - X^q)$), hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ asserting that the ring homomorphisms underlying $\overline{\alpha}$ and $\overline{\beta}$ for level $N$ and prime $q$ are integral, a place specialization $P$ for these data, a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$, an intermediate field $K$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, and a place $w$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ over $k$. Write $B = R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K\,w$ for the subring of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ consisting of those $f$ lying in $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegers}\,w$ whose Laurent series lies in $\mathrm{NodeLocalized.fieldOver}(Nq)\,K$, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ generated by the constant series of elements of $K$ together with $j_q$ and $j_{Nq}$. Assume $B$ is local and Noetherian, that every prime $\mathfrak p$ strictly contained in a prime $\mathfrak q \neq \mathfrak m_B$ is $\bot$ (so all non-maximal primes have height at most one), and that every $z \in \mathrm{NodeLocalized.fieldOver}(Nq)\,K$ can be written as $z\,y = x$ with $x, y \in B$, $y \neq 0$. Let $V, V'$ be places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ — valuation subrings containing $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, proper, with principal ideals — satisfying $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V = w = P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V'$, where $\mathrm{reduceFst}$ restricts a place along $\overline{\alpha}$ and then applies $P.\mathrm{sp}$. If $V.\mathrm{evalAt}\,g = V'.\mathrm{evalAt}\,g$ for every $g \in B$, then $V = V'$.
--
--   This is the separation statement for the two branches of the supersingular node: a place of the function field of $X_0(Nq)$ in characteristic zero lying over a given place $w$ downstairs is pinned down by its values on the node ring over $K$, the values of $j$ and $j_{Nq}$ alone being insufficient at a singular point of the plane model. It is used in the subsequent identification of products of values $V.\mathrm{evalAt}$ with norms from quotients of the node ring, and in the comparison with the local model of the crossing.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization_ProlongationTuple_eq_of_forall_evalAt_eq_of_reduceFst_eq.lean

